keywords:
  - bed exit
  - fall detection
  - depth camera
  - synthetic data
  - hospital
  - patient monitoring
  - pose estimation
  - Blender
  - AI-generated video
abstract: >-
  62 rendered clips of a hospital patient sitting up, leaving the bed, falling (eight kinds) or making
  look-alike movements, seen by a virtual depth camera on the wall in front of the bed with the fields of
  view of a Luxonis OAK-D Pro W. Each clip has a colour video, a grey infrared-like video, a 16-bit depth
  image per frame, exact event times, per-frame 3D body points with visibility flags, and the camera's
  calibration; 22 clips also have the empty room's depth. Includes locked baseline detection rules, their
  results, and the Blender pipeline that made the clips. A second part holds 52 AI-generated hospital
  videos from the same camera position (Wan 2.2, Veo 3.1 Fast, Seedance 2.0) and the 12 generated start
  pictures they begin from (Seedream 5.0 Pro), released as made.
